      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "Users with edit and export permission cannot pause, export, restore or permanently delete Grafana-managed recording rules from the rule list menu. This regresses behavior that worked before the list stopped calling the ruler API.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:public/app/features/alerting/unified/hooks/useAbilities.ts@sha256:bb99b902e7178713c1369e3126650167d57b228f800ee0f9ec8e54e3686d3fde"
        ],
        "explanation": "The ruler-based abilities gate ModifyExport, Pause, Restore and DeletePermanently on rulerRuleType.grafana.rule(rule), which is true for both alerting and recording Grafana rules. The new useAllGrafanaPromRuleAbilities gates the same actions on prometheusRuleType.grafana.alertingRule(rule), which is false for recording rules. The rule list now uses the prom-based path, and AlertRuleMenu ORs it with the ruler path. A Grafana recording rule shown in the list gets no pause or export entries, although it did in the ruler-based menu. No security bypass was found. The permission checks still use folder permissions, and the new path only narrows access.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 330,
          "start_line": 324
        },
