      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "Users see edit and delete actions on federated rule groups that were previously blocked. Those actions are not meant to be allowed, so the UI exposes them and the backend rejects them.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:public/app/features/alerting/unified/hooks/useAbilities.ts@sha256:bb99b902e7178713c1369e3126650167d57b228f800ee0f9ec8e54e3686d3fde",
          "target:target:sym:64d7bff6ec246a0d1df3c40f",
          "target:target:sym:377807a6d0e6976b142e9417"
        ],
        "explanation": "The old useAllAlertRuleAbilities computed isFederated = isFederatedRuleGroup(rule.group), which made federated Mimir rules immutable. The change makes it delegate to useAllRulerRuleAbilities, which hardcodes isFederated = false (TODO). The isFederatedRuleGroup import was also removed. For a CombinedRule in a federated group, immutableRule is now false. Update, Delete, Pause, Restore and DeletePermanently therefore report as supported, if the user has the permissions.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 245,
          "start_line": 242
        },
